WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Lift and downforce. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Set force direction and sign convention

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: Lift is defined relative to the flow; downforce describes a downward vertical force in the vehicle/road frame. Both depend on configuration.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Draw relative wind, then label the perpendicular force direction before deciding whether it is lift or downforce.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Force-vector labeling

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Simplified flow picture; real values need test method and conditions.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Set force direction and sign convention
